\section{Fourth order analysis of the disorder}\label{app:FourthOrder}

Here we explain the fourth order expansion of the metric components and the resulting Ricci curvature and trace anomaly equation.

Expanding the metric components to fourth order in $\epsilon,\bar{\epsilon}$ yields
\begin{subequations}
\begin{align}
    g_{tt}&=(-1+(\bar{\epsilon}-\epsilon)f+\epsilon\bar{\epsilon}f^2)\frac{1}{z^2}+\frac{\epsilon\bar{\epsilon}}{2}f^{\prime\,2},\\
