\subsection{Low-energy dynamics of a skyrmion}

In the absence of perturbations, the four conserved momenta (\ref{eq:momenta-conserved-BP-skyrmion}) of a BP skyrmion remain constant. The position, size, and global azimuthal spin angle do not change with time. Weak perturbations will induce slow motion of these collective variables. This low-energy dynamics can be captured by an effective theory with four collective coordinates $q = \{X, Y, \alpha, \Sigma\}$, whose time evolution is governed by Eq.~(\ref{eq:eom-general}). The gyroscopic tensor has nonzero components 
\begin{equation}
F_{XY} = -F_{YX} = - 4\pi \mathcal S,
\quad
F_{\alpha\Sigma} = - F_{\Sigma\alpha} = - \mathcal S.
\end{equation}
